Current original Zero workflow (0.12)

Use the native tools on Linux or their .exe versions on Windows:
  zero-integrate PROJECT_DIRECTORY NEW_KERNEL.zero
  zero-build PROJECT_DIRECTORY NEW_OUTPUT_DIRECTORY NEW_KERNEL.zero
  zero-check PROJECT_DIRECTORY NEW_TEST_DIRECTORY
All destination paths must be new. The integrator preserves authored sources;
the builder checks its compiler fixed point and builds the original targets;
the verifier checks language behavior and host file operations in process.
See tools/integrate.ztext, tools/build.ztext and checks/README.ztext.
Read these documents with zero-text read FILE.

The notes below preserve earlier implementation and test history. Any old
shell/Python runner names, generated artifacts, JSON reports or commands are
historical references: they were removed from the active project and are not
current runnable instructions or current-release validation. Native host
checks do not replace BIOS/UEFI, persistence or physical-hardware testing.

Historical implementation notes

Original Zero WiFi UI ABI, revision1, 2026-11-16

Ownership and integration
The wired worker owns a32KiB region at loader pool+0x28000. Its first24KiB
are wired network storage; the final8KiB are WiFi. console+2400 stores the
network base and console+2408 stores network base+24576. Both addresses must
be validated/published by kernel initialization before any WiFi snippet runs.
There is no additional reserve and no new top-level Zero variable. UI parts
reuse c0..c5,i,j,k,pointer,character,message. They never yield internally and
must run only in the terminal thread. Persistent state lives entirely in the
8KiB region. The PCI worker initializes discovery fields before publication.

Kernel integration calls these complete snippets:
  wifi-open.zero.part: preserve discovered cards, clear credentials and old
    request/results, enter detecting phase7, mark dirty. Does not render.
  wifi-step.zero.part: consume character as an event (set character=0), poll
    discovery/reply state, update phase and dirty. Event0 is a poll. One card
    automatically selects; two or more require selection. No shell echo.
  wifi-render.zero.part: produce45 columns x12 LF-terminated rows (552bytes)
    and NUL at WiFi+4648. Set message=WiFi+4096 and clear dirty. It reads no
    password byte; only length determines the visible stars/count.
  wifi-close.zero.part: wipe all64 secret bytes, clear length/request,
    invalidate pending replies, set phase0 and dirty. Consume character.

Root owns wifi command parsing, empty-argument validation, modal ownership,
PS/2 routing and original WM integration. While modal, suppress normal shell
echo and command editing. Extended scan-set1 make72=up and80=down map to256
and257. Escape make1 maps27. Enter13 or10 confirms; Backspace8/127 removes;
ASCII32..126 enters the password. Event0 polls completion. F-key window
actions are blocked during modal. Close/window destruction must run close
before releasing modal ownership, and restore the underlying terminal view.
The UI output may be sent to serial: it contains no secret. Do not send raw
input to serial, output history, or diagnostic dumps.

Root uses console+2416 modal flag and+2424 owner slot index. The UI does not
modify these. UI+80 is reserved for the owner field, also root-managed.

All following offsets are relative to the8KiB WiFi base. Header fields are
u64. Discovery worker writes only0,8 and card rows; UI owns remaining header
except backend response fields104,112 and network rows/count40.
 0 card count0..4;8 discovery busy0/1.
16 phase0closed,1card selection,2scan pending,3network selection,
   4password,5connect pending,6status,7automatic detection pending.
24 fixture marker:0production,1simulated backend. Production never sets1.
32 selected card, one-based;40 network count0..8;48 selected network1..8.
56 secret length0..63;64 request0none,1scan,2connect.
72 dirty0/1;80 root-owned modal owner;88 result/status code.
96 request generation;104 response generation;112 response code.
120 reserved.128..191 secret bytes, NUL-terminated, maximum63 ASCII bytes.
192..255 reserved (fixture harness uses200 for injected auth failure).
256..511: four64-byte PCI records, indexed with displayed card minus1.
  +0 PCI config address (0x80000000 plus BDF bits);+8 packed vendor/device
  u32 (vendor low16);+16 packed class/revision;+24 supported-driver0/1.
  +32..63 reserved. Shared PCI scan publishes actual class0280 controllers.
512..1023: eight64-byte network records, displayed network minus1.
  +0..32 SSID bytes followed byNUL, maximum32 bytes; display replaces any
  nonprintable/non-ASCII byte with question mark. Does not alter raw record.
  +40 security0open/1WPA2-PSK; +48 signal0..100; +56 reserved for BSSID.
1024..4095 reserved.4096..8191 UI output, currently553 bytes includingNUL.

Backend contract
UI publishes selected card/network and generation with request1 or2. In
this cooperative kernel snippets do not yield, so all fields are visible
before worker polling. Backend must validate every count/index. It fills
bounded network records and count for scan success, writes response code,
then publishes response generation LAST. UI accepts only its current
nonzero generation. Request remains nonzero until the matching reply is
consumed. No production backend is supplied yet; every discovered real
card must have supported-driver0, which prevents scan/connect requests.
Future drivers must implement actual association/security before reporting
connection success and must not infer it from interface/link readiness.
Closing/canceling sets request0 and advances generation. Backend must stop
an obsolete request and erase any private secret copies when canceled or
completed. A generation mismatch is not success. Scan response1 means scan
completed; zero networks then becomes status4. More than8 is scan failure.
Connect response1 means actual association/security success;5 means auth
rejected; other values fail. UI erases all64 secret bytes on every completed
connection, before publishing final status. IPv4/DNS/internet success is
separate from WiFi association and is not asserted by this interface.

Status codes:1connected,2no PCI radio,3unsupported controller,4no networks,
5auth rejected,6scan failed,7connection failed,8password shorter than8bytes.
Status8 remains on the password form; it never publishes a connect request.
No credential persistence or automatic reconnection is implemented.

Verification
Run python3 net/wifi-test.py from any directory. Python only assembles own
Zero source parts, invokes the own compiler/executable, supplies byte events,
asserts output, and losslessly encodes emitted PPM pixels as PNG when Pillow
is available. The actual state machine, mock backend, ASCII layout, font
rendering and pixel rendering execute compiled original Zero. PPM rendering
uses the current kernel's own5x7 font with a16x32 cell (UI scale2), at native
1920x1080. All mock-backend screens visibly identify SIMULATION/NO RADIO/
NO PACKETS. The hosted frame also visibly identifies HOSTED UI FIXTURE.
These files do not prove guest keyboard/framebuffer integration, packet
transport, radio scanning or authentication. Root VM tests own that boundary.
